IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`
IMPORT `crtpa-s3-variation`

-- Tests for section 3.  Every expected value is written from the text of s 3, with the reason beside it,
-- before the module was run.  In each call the inputs are, in order, those of the rule's GIVEN.

§ `Tests -- s 3(1)(a), (b), (c): the circumstances`

#ASSERT `s 3(1)(a) the third party has communicated the third party's assent to the term to the promisor` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(a) the third party has communicated the third party's assent to the term to the promisor` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b) the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the term` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b) the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the term` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (c): foreseen (a judgment stated by the person) AND in fact relied.
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term and the third party has in fact relied on it` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term and the third party has in fact relied on it` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term and the third party has in fact relied on it` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term and the third party has in fact relied on it` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term and the third party has in fact relied on it` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(whether or not the third party has knowledge of its precise terms)": knowledge is no condition of (b) or (c).
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b) and (c) knowledge of the precise terms of the term is a condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b) and (c) knowledge of the precise terms of the term is a condition` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) OR (b) OR (c); inputs: (a) assent communicated, (b) promisor aware of reliance, (c) foreseen, in fact relied.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests -- s 3(2): the assent`

#ASSERT `s 3(2)(a) the assent may be by this form` `words` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(a) the assent may be by this form` `conduct` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(a) the assent may be by this form` `silence or inaction` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(a) the assent may be by this form` `some other form` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b), inputs: sent by post or other means; received by the promisor.  The bar: not regarded as communicated until received.
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) the assent cannot yet be regarded as communicated to the promisor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) the assent cannot yet be regarded as communicated to the promisor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) the assent cannot yet be regarded as communicated to the promisor` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) the assent cannot yet be regarded as communicated to the promisor` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Act never says the assent HAS been communicated: JUST FALSE before receipt, NOTHING after it.
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) the assent has been communicated to the promisor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) the assent has been communicated to the promisor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) the assent has been communicated to the promisor` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) the assent has been communicated to the promisor` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 3(1): the bar on the parties`

-- inputs: the third party has a right under s 2; what the parties do; the third party has consented; one circumstance exists.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `vary the contract in such a way as to extinguish or alter the third party's entitlement` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a variation that neither extinguishes nor alters the entitlement, and a change not by agreement, are outside the bar.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `vary the contract in some other way` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `change the contract otherwise than by agreement of the parties` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "without the third party's consent": with consent the bar does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST FALSE) `rescind the contract` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST FALSE) `vary the contract in some other way` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "where a third party has a right under section 2": no right, no bar.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST FALSE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST FALSE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "if (a), (b) or (c)": none of them, no bar.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` NOTHING `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not stated.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` NOTHING `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 3(3): express terms of the contract`

-- inputs: right; what the parties do; consented; one circumstance exists; the express term; the circumstances the contract specifies exist.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `no such express term` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3)(a): the contract lets the parties rescind or vary without the consent: the bar does not bite.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `a term under which the parties may rescind or vary without the third party's consent` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `a term under which the parties may rescind or vary without the third party's consent` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3)(a) lifts only a bar that (1) imposes; where (1) says nothing it still says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` (JUST TRUE) `vary the contract in some other way` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `a term under which the parties may rescind or vary without the third party's consent` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(b): the circumstances the contract specifies take the place of (a), (b) and (c).
#ASSERT `s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `a term requiring the third party's consent in circumstances specified in the contract instead of those in section 3(1)(a), (b) and (c)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `a term requiring the third party's consent in circumstances specified in the contract instead of those in section 3(1)(a), (b) and (c)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` TRUE (JUST TRUE) `a term requiring the third party's consent in circumstances specified in the contract instead of those in section 3(1)(a), (b) and (c)` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` (JUST FALSE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `a term requiring the third party's consent in circumstances specified in the contract instead of those in section 3(1)(a), (b) and (c)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 3(4) to (7): dispensing with the consent`

-- (4), inputs: consent required under (1) or (3); the parties applied; satisfied (a) whereabouts; satisfied (b) mentally incapable.
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5), inputs: the consent may be required under (1)(c); the parties applied; satisfied that reliance cannot reasonably be ascertained.
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with a consent that may be required under subsection (1)(c)` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with a consent that may be required under subsection (1)(c)` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with a consent that may be required under subsection (1)(c)` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with a consent that may be required under subsection (1)(c)` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with a consent that may be required under subsection (1)(c)` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with a consent that may be required under subsection (1)(c)` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6), input: the court or tribunal has dispensed with the consent.
#ASSERT `s 3(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may impose such conditions as it thinks fit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may impose such conditions as it thinks fit` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may impose a condition requiring the payment of compensation to the third party` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may impose a condition requiring the payment of compensation to the third party` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (7): "exercisable by both the General Division of the High Court and a District Court".
#ASSERT `s 3(7) the jurisdiction conferred on the court by subsections (4), (5) and (6) is exercisable by this body` `the General Division of the High Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(7) the jurisdiction conferred on the court by subsections (4), (5) and (6) is exercisable by this body` `a District Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(7) the jurisdiction conferred on the court by subsections (4), (5) and (6) is exercisable by this body` `another court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(7) the jurisdiction conferred on the court by subsections (4), (5) and (6) is exercisable by this body` `an arbitral tribunal` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Assertions on the regulative rules where nothing stands (FULFILLED)`

-- On this binary a DEONTIC value can be compared in an #ASSERT only when it is FULFILLED; a rule that leaves an obligation or a
-- permission standing gives eval/unsupported-equality (probed 2026-11-05), so those outcomes are the traces below, read by eye.
-- s 3(1): the third party has no right under s 2: nothing is prohibited.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract SHANT rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST FALSE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `no such express term` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 3(1) with (3)(a): the contract itself lets the parties rescind without consent: nothing is prohibited.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract SHANT rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `a term under which the parties may rescind or vary without the third party's consent` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 3(1): the third party has consented: the prohibition does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the parties to the contract SHANT rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` TRUE (JUST TRUE) `no such express term` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 3(4): the parties have not applied: no power, nothing standing.
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal MAY dispense with the third party's consent` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS FULFILLED

§ `Traces -- the regulative rules where something stands (read by eye)`

-- s 3(1): the bar applies.  The parties rescind at time 1: a breach of the prohibition.
#TRACE `s 3(1) the parties to the contract SHANT rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `no such express term` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the parties to the contract` DOES `rescind the contract by agreement without the third party's consent` AT 1
-- the bar applies and the parties do nothing: the prohibition stands.
#TRACE `s 3(1) the parties to the contract SHANT rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `no such express term` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)
-- the bar does not apply (the third party has no right under s 2): nothing is prohibited, so the rule is fulfilled.
#TRACE `s 3(1) the parties to the contract SHANT rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST FALSE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `no such express term` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the parties to the contract` DOES `rescind the contract by agreement without the third party's consent` AT 1
-- the contract itself lets the parties rescind (s 3(3)(a)): nothing is prohibited.
#TRACE `s 3(1) the parties to the contract SHANT rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` (JUST TRUE) `rescind the contract` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `a term under which the parties may rescind or vary without the third party's consent` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the parties to the contract` DOES `rescind the contract by agreement without the third party's consent` AT 1
-- s 3(4): the power exists, the court dispenses with the consent: the permission is used.
#TRACE `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal MAY dispense with the third party's consent` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court or arbitral tribunal` DOES `dispense with the third party's consent` AT 2
-- s 3(4): no application, no power: fulfilled with nothing standing.
#TRACE `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal MAY dispense with the third party's consent` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)
